        <div class="fc-delta-reason">September 23 polls: Channel 12 (Yashar 23, Likud 20), KAN News (Yashar 24, Likud 20), Channel 13 (Yashar 22, Likud 18), i24NEWS outlier (Likud 27, Yashar 22). Average across four surveys: Yashar 22.2, Likud 21.2 seats. Eisenkot bloc holds ~54 seats vs. Netanyahu bloc ~50; neither reaches the 61-seat majority threshold. Hendel-Zelekha and Amcha Israel hover near the 3.25% threshold &#8212; their presence or absence shifts several bloc seats. Netanyahu&#8217;s Sep 24 UNGA address had not landed as of filing. P revised from 0.42 to 0.37 reflecting Yashar&#8217;s consistent polling lead while preserving substantial probability mass for the competitive race.</div>
